# Weather and fog cross from the host; a fog patch's foglets are one set of creatures for both players. Hero 5 slot 0.
# A client freezes its own weather and glides to the host's levels. A patch wakes its foglets on the machine whose
# player walks in, at a random tick. Patch _16 (-749,-6380) spawns only when foggy.

include session.coop

# Foglets down a fresh hero quickly; two down is a lost run.
A run invincibility
B run invincibility

# ---- Levels: the host's cheat moves the client's sky, and back. ----
A run fog 3
A expect weather contains "fog=3 " timeout=5
B expect weather contains "fog=3 " timeout=20
B expect weather contains enabled=0 timeout=1
A run rain 2
B expect weather contains "rain=2 " timeout=20
A run rain 0
B expect weather contains "rain=0 " timeout=20

# ---- Foglets: both players walk into a fog patch in the fog. ----
A tp -749,-6380
B tp -700,-6400
sleep 5
A walk 1 0 0.5
B walk -1 0 0.5
A expect foglets 600 contains "active=" timeout=10
A foglets 600
B foglets 600
# The patch wakes at a random tick, then fades in: give it time.
A expect foglets 600 contains "mode=Active" timeout=90
B expect foglets 600 contains "mode=Active" timeout=30
A foglets 600
B foglets 600
A actors 800
B actors 800

# ---- Both fight them: every foglet killed on the host dies for the client, the patch beaten on both. ----
A ?hit Foglet 5000
B ?hit Foglet 5000
A ?hit Foglet 5000
B ?hit Foglet 5000
A ?hit Foglet 5000
B ?hit Foglet 5000
A ?hit Foglet 5000
B ?hit Foglet 5000
A ?hit Foglet 5000
B ?hit Foglet 5000
A ?hit Foglet 5000
B ?hit Foglet 5000
sleep 5
A foglets 600
B foglets 600
A expect foglets 600 contains "defeated=1" timeout=30
B expect foglets 600 contains "defeated=1" timeout=30

# ---- Only the host walks into patch _15; the client watches from outside, so what it sees is the host's. ----
A tp -90,-6793
B tp -90,-6150
sleep 5
A walk 1 0 0.5
A expect foglets 400 contains "mode=Active" timeout=90
sleep 3
A foglets 400
B foglets 800
A actors 500
B actors 800
B expect actors 800 contains Foglet timeout=15
# The client is well outside the patch: its copy can only have woken because the host's did.
B expect counter fogletwoken >= 1 timeout=10
B expect foglets 800 contains "mode=Active" timeout=10
# The foglets' fog duplicates: spawned by the host, shared, built on the client from the host's word.
A expect counter spawnshared >= 1 timeout=90
B expect actors 800 contains Foglet_Minion timeout=15
A counter spawnshared
B counter spawnskipped

# ---- Thunder: the host's storm rolls the strikes, the client plays exactly those and none of its own. ----
A run thunder 2
B expect weather contains "thunder=2 " timeout=20
A expect counter thundersent >= 2 timeout=90
B expect counter thundershown >= 2 timeout=10
capture sent A counter thundersent
B expect counter thundershown == $sent timeout=10
A shot
B shot
A run thunder 0
B expect weather contains "thunder=0 " timeout=20
# ---- Clearing: the host's fog lifts on the client too. ----
A run fog 0
A expect weather contains "fog=0 " timeout=10
B expect weather contains "fog=0 " timeout=20
B expect weather contains enabled=0 timeout=1
